1
00:00:18,357 --> 00:00:21,527
When you think of Cape Cod
you probably think of beaches...

2
00:00:21,861 --> 00:00:24,614
lobster, little fishing villages.

3
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:28,493
Well, I grew up here, and
I mostly think of baseball.

4
00:00:31,623 --> 00:00:35,168
The best amateur ball in the country
is played in the Cape Cod Baseball League.

5
00:00:35,293 --> 00:00:37,796
Playing here is the chance of a lifetime.

6
00:00:39,507 --> 00:00:42,636
I've been mowing this field in Chatham
since I was 14.

7
00:00:42,719 --> 00:00:45,680
But this summer it feels a little different.

8
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:52,105
If you're a college player like me, the Cape
is where you want to go for the summer.

9
00:00:52,188 --> 00:00:56,359
Little towns like Yarmouth and Dennis,
Wareham and Chatham.

10
00:00:56,443 --> 00:00:59,487
Families open their homes to kids
from all over the country...

11
00:00:59,613 --> 00:01:02,908
who come to show their stuff
to big league scouts.

12
00:01:02,993 --> 00:01:05,412
Hi, I'm Billy Brubaker. 
This is Miles...

13
00:01:05,495 --> 00:01:07,372
Dalrymple. Love y'all's house.

14
00:01:08,249 --> 00:01:09,541
So, how's the surf?

15
00:01:10,459 --> 00:01:13,337
Some of us are farther away from home
than we've ever been.

16
00:01:13,714 --> 00:01:17,467
Staying with people who have
strange ideas about being a house parent.

17
00:01:17,718 --> 00:01:19,262
Are you hungry, honey?

18
00:01:20,805 --> 00:01:23,307
Come here, I have something for you.

19
00:01:25,728 --> 00:01:29,398
They say one in six big leaguers played
in the Cape League.

20
00:01:29,565 --> 00:01:32,277
I can't count all the ones 
I've seen play on this field.

21
00:01:32,444 --> 00:01:38,576
Bagwell, Bell, Biggio, 
Nomar, Mo Vaughn, the Big Hurt.

22
00:01:41,204 --> 00:01:45,042
I've watched so many dreams
come true and die...

23
00:01:45,167 --> 00:01:47,586
on the ball fields of the Cape.

24
00:01:47,753 --> 00:01:51,507
Hard as it is to believe, 
now it's my turn.

25
00:01:52,508 --> 00:01:55,261
Now I'm the guy the scouts 
will be watching.

26
00:01:56,555 --> 00:02:00,392
Now I'm the guy putting it on the line
every time I take the mound.

27
00:02:03,813 --> 00:02:06,023
This is my last shot to make it.

28
00:02:06,859 --> 00:02:09,278
The last house on the block,
you might say.

29
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:17,871
While it might be an advantage
to sleep in my own bed...

30
00:02:18,038 --> 00:02:22,293
the night before the first team meeting,
I figured I'd leave nothing to chance.

31
00:02:22,377 --> 00:02:25,214
I've been accused of being 
my own worst enemy.

32
00:02:25,297 --> 00:02:28,008
So this time I wanted to focus...

33
00:02:28,092 --> 00:02:31,471
to make sure nothing got in the way
of the most important summer of my life.

34
00:02:33,223 --> 00:02:34,766
Good morning, Sunshine.

35
00:02:37,645 --> 00:02:39,104
All right, come on!

36
00:02:42,066 --> 00:02:44,819
Look. No offense, Dede,
but I can't do this tonight.

37
00:02:45,654 --> 00:02:48,281
Ryan, where's your team spirit?

38
00:02:48,407 --> 00:02:50,785
I'm dressed for practice tomorrow, man.

39
00:02:50,869 --> 00:02:53,545
I'm dressed for practice.

40
00:02:52,579 --> 00:02:56,000
I'm staying here tonight. 
I can't be late.

41
00:02:56,625 --> 00:02:57,667
That's cool.

42
00:02:58,168 --> 00:03:01,714
Sorry. We just
wanted to celebrate our buddy.

43
00:03:01,716 --> 00:03:05,760
Local boy playing for the Chatham A's
with all those fancy college kids.

44
00:03:07,555 --> 00:03:09,807
We're very proud of you, Ryan.

45
00:03:10,057 --> 00:03:14,520
I'm serious! I made a vow
to swear off women and beer.

46
00:03:14,771 --> 00:03:17,690
Y'all gotta get out of here. Go.

47
00:03:18,108 --> 00:03:20,777
All right, we're out. 
Let's go, come on.

48
00:03:24,533 --> 00:03:26,910
It's your last chance, lawn boy.

49
00:03:28,287 --> 00:03:31,165
Because I'll be working
on the vineyard all summer long.

50
00:03:31,541 --> 00:03:38,006
I just want you to take a good, hard look
at exactly what you're passing up on.

51
00:03:39,508 --> 00:03:42,052
So as you spend the rest of your life...

52
00:03:42,471 --> 00:03:46,933
riding that mower up and down
the great grass of the Cape.

53
00:03:48,227 --> 00:03:51,981
l want you to have that one...

54
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:56,394
burning image in your mind
of the one that got away.

55
00:03:59,073 --> 00:04:02,452
All right.
One beer. That's it.

56
00:04:02,702 --> 00:04:04,954
Can I do our special style?

57
00:04:05,705 --> 00:04:07,290
Special style.

58
00:04:13,382 --> 00:04:14,633
Domo, honey.

59
00:04:15,676 --> 00:04:17,594
Are you awake?

60
00:04:24,812 --> 00:04:27,898
Domo, I know you're not sleeping.

61
00:04:29,149 --> 00:04:33,737
Okay. Sleep tight.
Don't let the bed bugs bite.

62
00:04:38,077 --> 00:04:39,912
I've got to get some sleep.

63
00:04:41,789 --> 00:04:42,874
