Like this, "Welcome."

478
00:37:43,099 --> 00:37:44,809
"Welcome to failure."

479
00:37:45,268 --> 00:37:46,686
He wants you to fail?

480
00:37:46,770 --> 00:37:48,481
He did. My brother did.

481
00:37:49,899 --> 00:37:52,276
Forget them. What do you want?

482
00:37:56,782 --> 00:37:58,033
I want to make it.

483
00:37:59,034 --> 00:38:00,953
I want to play pro ball.

484
00:38:02,663 --> 00:38:06,626
Then you will.
You just have to allow yourself to succeed.

485
00:38:10,673 --> 00:38:15,011
You want big rewards,
you've got to take big risks.

486
00:38:43,545 --> 00:38:45,713
Don't worry, Bru,
I'm a licensed professional.

487
00:38:49,343 --> 00:38:51,511
You got the Dede Mulligan
midnight special!

488
00:38:57,602 --> 00:39:00,188
Are you still mad we missed 
the bus?

489
00:39:03,151 --> 00:39:07,406
I don't know if you paid attention,
but the Big Bad Bru is back...

490
00:39:08,323 --> 00:39:10,992
and he's all nuded up.

491
00:39:31,851 --> 00:39:33,686
She was awesome.

492
00:39:34,062 --> 00:39:36,315
She made the grapes disappear.

493
00:39:37,441 --> 00:39:39,067
What grapes?

494
00:39:39,318 --> 00:39:41,069
I'll see you tonight, buddy.

495
00:39:47,327 --> 00:39:49,455
Domo, good morning.

496
00:39:49,747 --> 00:39:50,998
Time to get up.

497
00:39:53,377 --> 00:39:55,754
I made something special for you.

498
00:40:01,219 --> 00:40:04,138
- When is your next start?
- I don't know.

499
00:40:09,103 --> 00:40:10,687
Thinking about pitching?

500
00:40:11,146 --> 00:40:12,815
What else would I be 
thinking about?

501
00:40:14,651 --> 00:40:16,944
Rand Parrish's daughter.

502
00:40:19,532 --> 00:40:21,158
You don't know what you're 
talking about.

503
00:40:24,538 --> 00:40:27,290
You're setting yourself up for a big fall.

504
00:40:27,416 --> 00:40:30,545
Yeah, I know.
Shore Road princess.

505
00:40:36,427 --> 00:40:38,637
- You slept late today.
- She was out late.

506
00:40:38,971 --> 00:40:40,681
With Ryan Dunne.

507
00:40:40,398 --> 00:40:41,198
Who?

508
00:40:41,808 --> 00:40:45,311
Super cute southpaw.
Got a shot if he can harness that temper.

509
00:40:46,771 --> 00:40:48,523
The kid who cuts the grass?

510
00:40:49,900 --> 00:40:51,300
Sean Dunne is a good landscaper...

511
00:40:51,501 --> 00:40:54,802
but his kid is a little rough
around the edges, don't you think?

512
00:40:54,823 --> 00:40:59,035
- Relax, Rand.
- There's nothing going on.

513
00:41:02,123 --> 00:41:06,086
Charlie Hunt called. He and his wife
are planning a trip up to the Cape.

514
00:41:07,046 --> 00:41:09,882
I told you Chris and I
are taking some time off this summer.

515
00:41:09,965 --> 00:41:12,927
Does that mean his parents
can't plan a vacation?

516
00:41:13,803 --> 00:41:17,139
No, but I'm sure
that you invited them to Chatham.

517
00:41:17,149 --> 00:41:19,277
He did, but don't worry, 
they can't make it.

518
00:41:20,227 --> 00:41:23,027
Chris got on the phone to say hello
and we chatted for a minute.

519
00:41:22,942 --> 00:41:25,443
I invited him up for a game of golf.

520
00:41:26,943 --> 00:41:29,738
He'll be here on the 25th.

521
00:41:32,450 --> 00:41:34,702
Tenley, don't overreact.
Your father and Chris...

522
00:41:34,786 --> 00:41:36,955
We like to play golf. 
What's the big deal?

523
00:41:37,039 --> 00:41:40,375
Great, Dad. Then you marry him,
because I'm not ready to.

524
00:42:00,817 --> 00:42:01,859
Dad.

525
00:42:03,611 --> 00:42:07,157
This is Billy Brubaker,
our catcher.

526
00:42:15,291 --> 00:42:18,044
So you met Dede Mulligan 
last night?

527
00:42:19,380 --> 00:42:21,131
Yeah, I like Dede.

528
00:42:23,677 --> 00:42:24,928
Nice thong.

529
00:42:28,390 --> 00:42:29,308
Thanks.

530
00:42:34,276 --> 00:42:39,778
Domo, come here, honey.

531
00:42:41,113 --> 00:42:42,907
I have something for you.

532
00:42:45,869 --> 00:42:47,120
I'm going to sleep now.

533
00:42:52,252 --> 00:42:54,837
Marjorie, I'm ready.

534
00:42:55,213 --> 00:42:59,801
I'll be right out, Miles. Read me
that poem you wrote for me again.

535
00:43:00,845 --> 00:43:02,179
I can do that.

536
00:43:08,479 --> 00:43:11,106
"She is large and she is hot,...

537
00:43:11,775 --> 00:43:15,153
she's in charge
and I am not.

538
00:43:17,782 --> 00:43:20,075
She consumes me with her size,...

539
00:43:20,910 --> 00:43:22,578
cannot believe my eyes.

540
00:43:24,748 --> 00:43:26,708
I so love her shapely belly,...

541
00:43:28,376 --> 00:43:30,629
that moves around like grapely jelly.

542
00:43:33,049 --> 00:43:36,678
I wish that there was more of me
so I could love more Marjorie."

543
00:43:50,736 --> 00:43:52,738
Nothing better than swimming 
in the rain.

544
00:43:52,905 --> 00:43:54,240
Excuse me?

545
00:44:06,463 --> 00:44:08,965
- What are you doing?
- Finally got you to chase me.

546
00:44:09,258 --> 00:44:10,842
Aren't your parents home?

547
00:44:10,926 --> 00:44:14,013
Yeah. So? I'm not
allowed to swim in my own pool?

548
00:44:18,519 --> 00:44:20,729
You're not going to make me 
swim alone, are you?

549
00:44:43,089 --> 00:44:44,840
Swimming in the rain.

550
00:44:50,832 --> 00:44:52,912
You were thinking about kissing me, 
weren't you?

551
00:44:52,770 --> 00:44:53,521
No!

552
00:44:54,895 --> 00:44:57,230
Now that I said that,
you're thinking about it.

553
00:44:57,314 --> 00:44:58,940
No, I'm thinking that's what 
you're thinking.

554
00:44:59,024 --> 00:45:01,819
No, I think I can swim the length
and back underwater.

555
00:45:01,903 --> 00:45:04,071
- $5 says you can't.
- You got it.

556
00:45:24,805 --> 00:45:26,097
Who's out there?

557
00:45:28,100 --> 00:45:30,019
Vivi, get me a flashlight!

558
00:45:53,422 --> 00:45:55,006
You owe me $5.

559
00:45:55,841 --> 00:45:57,008
Stay right where you are!

560
00:46:07,952 --> 00:46:10,412
God, the car! Vivi, 
call the police!

561
00:46:24,273 --> 00:46:26,275
If my father catches us, 
he'll kill us!

562
00:46:27,193 --> 00:46:28,694
No, he'll kill me.

563
00:46:30,780 --> 00:46:32,490
Am I going to see you 
tomorrow night?

564
00:46:33,325 --> 00:46:35,703
Yeah, of course. You don't think
your dad really called the cops, do you?

565
00:46:36,913 --> 00:46:38,497
Yeah, I'm sure he did.

566
00:46:40,041 --> 00:46:42,961
He'd really have me handcuffed
and thrown in the back of a cop car?

567
00:46:43,445 --> 00:46:46,239
No, he'd have you beaten
and dragged first.

568
00:46:48,551 --> 00:46:50,360
- Okay, then I'm going to go.
- Okay.

569
00:46:55,025 --> 00:46:56,125
- Bye
- Bye.

570
00:47:00,315 --> 00:47:02,108
Billy Brubaker steps in...

571
00:47:02,817 --> 00:47:04,985
still looking for his first hit.

572
00:47:05,488 --> 00:47:09,200
Sometimes you need a little sunshine
to help break the ice.

573
00:47:24,115 --> 00:47:24,965
Safe!

574
00:47:28,389 --> 00:47:32,185
Billy Brubaker has just gotten his first hit
of the Cape League season.

575
00:47:33,311 --> 00:47:36,023
Now he's grabbing the ball
out of Seaver's hand as a keepsake.

576
00:47:44,950 --> 00:47:48,329
The A's visit the Yarmouth-Dennis
Red Sox today, and before the game...

577
00:47:48,913 --> 00:47:52,416
Billy Brubaker told me it's nice
to finally have a batting average.

578
00:47:55,087 --> 00:47:57,798
Bru's average is climbing every 
day now.

579
00:48:00,427 --> 00:48:02,929
All the way up now to .268.

580
00:48:13,567 --> 00:48:18,447
The hometown lefty, Ryan Dunne,
continues his Jekyll-and-Hyde ways.

581
00:49:00,280 --> 00:49:01,595
Strike three!

582
00:49:02,249 --> 00:49:04,125
You are out of there!

583
00:49:05,878 --> 00:49:07,004
Give me the ball.

584
00:49:51,347 --> 00:49:53,475
All right! Way to go!

585
00:49:54,351 --> 00:49:56,861
I'm proud of you guys.
You're making me look good out there.

586
00:49:57,813 --> 00:50:00,358
Ryan, you get to start Saturday
against Hyannis.

587
00:50:01,484 --> 00:50:03,611
You know what they say about 
us lefties?

588
00:50:03,737 --> 00:50:06,782
The Earth's gravitational force
is in our favor. It makes our pitches dance.

589
00:50:07,241 --> 00:50:09,034
Dunne is going to get lit up.

590
00:50:11,663 --> 00:50:12,914
Lawn boy.

591
00:50:13,707 --> 00:50:15,166
Hope you're ready.

592
00:50:15,250 --> 00:50:16,292
For what?

593
00:50:17,795 --> 00:50:23,176
Hyannis. It's the best lineup in the League.
You got two guys batting over .400.

594
00:50:23,552 --> 00:50:26,638
Both of them first rounders,
solid gold bonus babies.

595
00:50:27,139 --> 00:50:28,181
Yeah. So?

596
00:50:28,807 --> 00:50:31,644
So everyone in that lineup
can take your yard.

597
00:50:32,103 --> 00:50:34,396
Every scout in the country
is going to be there.

598
00:50:34,773 --> 00:50:38,527
I'd think twice before inviting the friends.
It could get embarrassing.

599
00:50:38,694 --> 00:50:39,736
Come on, man.

600
00:50:43,998 --> 00:50:45,411
There you go.

601
00:50:47,037 --> 00:50:50,082
I'm starting against Hyannis 
on Saturday.

602
00:50:50,166 --> 00:50:52,668
They got two first rounders
that tear the cover off the ball.

603
00:50:53,295 --> 00:50:56,506
- What inning should I show up for?
- What?

604
00:50:57,716 --> 00:50:59,969
I should probably get there
pretty early, right?

605
00:51:06,269 --> 00:51:08,145
Hey, man, what's that supposed 
to mean?

606
00:51:09,038 --> 00:51:11,750
I'm just trying to figure out
what inning you'll self-destruct.

607
00:51:11,746 --> 00:51:13,746
I want to be there for that.

608
00:51:14,194 --> 00:51:15,778
Why aren't you behind me?

609
00:51:16,905 --> 00:51:20,409
I'm behind you. Everyone is
behind you, except you.

610
00:51:22,328 --> 00:51:24,039
Just because you didn't have
what it takes...

611
00:51:24,123 --> 00:51:28,127
I didn't have it!
I never had it, but you do.

612
00:51:28,669 --> 00:51:32,298
You got a bag full of talent
and a head full of crap.

613
00:51:32,799 --> 00:51:35,594
Ever since Mom died,
you think the world owes you something.

614
00:51:35,678 --> 00:51:38,898
Bullshit! You've been given this gift.

615
00:51:38,823 --> 00:51:40,323
You just piss it away.

616
00:51:45,022 --> 00:51:46,732
I'm tired of this shit.

617
00:51:59,225 --> 00:52:00,775
- Hi.
- Hey.

618
00:52:03,348 --> 00:52:04,848
I'm sorry it's so late.

619
00:52:05,963 --> 00:52:08,173
I just really needed to see you.

620
00:52:09,300 --> 00:52:11,970
I told you I couldn't see 
you tonight.

621
00:52:12,054 --> 00:52:15,557
I know. I got this fight with my brother
and I'm just feeling a little spun.

622
00:52:16,610 --> 00:52:19,437
Hey. I'm Chris Hunt.

623
00:52:19,315 --> 00:52:20,259
Tenley!

624
00:52:21,584 --> 00:52:22,628
I am...

625
00:52:22,690 --> 00:52:26,403
Ryan, the gardener's son.
Why are you here at this time of night?

626
00:52:26,487 --> 00:52:28,487
It's late. My dad had asked me to...

627
00:52:28,494 --> 00:52:30,155
Come in, have a beer.

628
00:52:31,034 --> 00:52:32,994
- You know my daughter Tenley, I believe.
- Yes, sir.

629
00:52:39,204 --> 00:52:42,208
So Ryan, you were about to 
tell us why you stopped by.

630
00:52:45,753 --> 00:52:49,132
My dad asked me
to check on the hydrangeas.

631
00:52:50,926 --> 00:52:53,179
He was worried
that they weren't blooming.

632
00:52:54,305 --> 00:52:56,640
So you work for Rand?

633
00:52:57,100 --> 00:53:00,521
Ryan and his father
do splendid landscaping.

634
00:53:04,358 --> 00:53:06,110
I cut the grass.

635
00:53:07,862 --> 00:53:10,406
I really have to go. 
Thank you.

636
00:53:11,742 --> 00:53:12,993
I'll see him out.

637
00:53:18,500 --> 00:53:20,001
Son of a bitch!

638
00:53:21,169 --> 00:53:23,505
What the fuck was I thinking? 
This is crazy!

639
00:53:23,840 --> 00:53:25,675
I'm about to pitch
the biggest game of my life.

640
00:53:26,092 --> 00:53:28,511
- I know you are. 
And you're going to be great.
- Bullshit!

641
00:53:28,886 --> 00:53:31,848
His name is Chris Hunt. We decided
not to see each other this summer.

642
00:53:31,932 --> 00:53:34,643
My father invited him
to play golf without asking me.

643
00:53:34,727 --> 00:53:38,928
Really? lf you would be asked, would you say
Ryan would love to play croquet tennis...

644
00:53:38,868 --> 00:53:41,569
or maybe have martinis at the 
Yacht Club?

645
00:53:41,652 --> 00:53:43,779
I haven't really told my parents 
about you.

646
00:53:43,863 --> 00:53:45,781
And you didn't tell me
about Chris.

647
00:53:46,782 --> 00:53:50,119
I told Chris I needed to take
this summer off.

648
00:53:50,287 --> 00:53:54,208
Everybody is pressuring me. My father
is pushing me to go to San Francisco.

649
00:53:55,627 --> 00:53:58,630
I just wanted to do nothing
for the summer.

650
00:54:02,710 --> 00:54:03,560
Yeah.

651
00:54:03,969 --> 00:54:06,138
And I'm the nothing you picked.

652
00:54:07,265 --> 00:54:09,475
- Ryan, listen to me.
- No.

653
00:54:10,018 --> 00:54:12,980
Let's go back to:
I'm the guy who cuts your father's grass.

654
00:54:13,064 --> 00:54:14,774
Everybody is more comfortable 
that way.

655
00:54:15,608 --> 00:54:18,403
That's not fair. Ryan, I'm sorry.

656
00:54:26,204 --> 00:54:27,663
Hey, Miles.

657
00:54:35,298 --> 00:54:37,133
That is unhealthy.

658
00:54:37,467 --> 00:54:39,010
Can we not do this again?

659
00:54:39,427 --> 00:54:41,513
Domo, don't you think that's
unhealthy?

660
00:54:42,181 --> 00:54:45,123
You think all sex is unhealthy.
Never mind.

661
00:54:45,726 --> 00:54:51,048
What I'm saying is, Miles, these women
are too big to be fooling with.

662
00:54:51,817 --> 00:54:56,280
I'm afraid in the heat of passion one of them
will roll over on you. Squash you dead.

663
00:55:00,244 --> 00:55:01,370
Ryan, hold up a second.

664
00:55:04,331 --> 00:55:06,292
Did you go over the lineup?

665
00:55:07,085 --> 00:55:09,587
The number four and number 
five batters are red-hot.

666
00:55:10,529 --> 00:55:14,830
The four guy, he jumps on the first pitch
and five sits on breaking stuff.

667
00:55:18,390 --> 00:55:21,893
You know, I was a pitcher at 
Florida State for three years.

668
00:55:23,187 --> 00:55:26,565
I had a cup of coffee with
the Twins. Half a cup.

669
00:55:28,986 --> 00:55:33,986
When you're a pitcher you got to pray
that your stuff will show up.

670
00:55:36,369 --> 00:55:39,530
Then one day you have this moment
where it all just arrives. 

671
00:55:39,698 --> 00:55:41,609
Everything clicks.

672
00:55:41,658 --> 00:55:46,878
Command, control, velocity.
You feel invincible.

673
00:55:48,634 --> 00:55:50,636
You'll spend many nights
out there looking for it.

674
00:55:51,887 --> 00:55:54,307
But once you've found it,
just once, it's yours.

675
00:55:56,142 --> 00:55:59,104
You have it inside you,
and you know you have it.

676
00:56:00,606 --> 00:56:04,016
It gives you the strength
to go out there night after night...

677
00:56:03,995 --> 00:56:06,383
and face those sons of bitches.

678
00:56:13,037 --> 00:56:16,950
Holding your breath underwater and 
go-cart racing will never be Olympic events.

679
00:56:17,194 --> 00:56:18,285
Why not?

680
00:56:20,671 --> 00:56:23,466
Go get them. You're wicked awesome.
Ry in the game tonight, baby.

681
00:56:24,926 --> 00:56:25,968
Wait!

682
00:56:26,219 --> 00:56:28,012
What if I cut my left arm off?

683
00:56:28,388 --> 00:56:31,392
Do you think they'd let me compete
in the Special Olympics?

684
00:56:31,558 --> 00:56:33,476
I'd really love to win a medal.

685
00:56:34,495 --> 00:56:39,359
Pete, why don't you go sit by the garbage
and think about what you just said, okay?

686
00:56:39,901 --> 00:56:43,361
You need to go, bud.
That's messed up, Pete.

687
00:56:45,574 --> 00:56:47,618
Hey, fish girl, get out of here.

688
00:56:49,621 --> 00:56:53,125
Go. Get out of here. 
Take a hike.

689
00:56:59,091 --> 00:57:02,844
Still scoreless as the Hyannis Mets
come to bat in the top of the fourth.

690
00:57:04,638 --> 00:57:07,449
Say, Dick, what do you make
of this kid, Dunne?

691
00:57:08,184 --> 00:57:11,644
- Good fast ball, bad mechanics.
- But there's something about him.

692
00:57:11,653 --> 00:57:15,874
He's throwing that heavy ball and
a heavy ball ain't going to find many bats.

693
00:57:17,112 --> 00:57:19,989
- I'll see you tomorrow.
- Yeah, you will.

694
00:57:22,553 --> 00:57:24,597
One down now. Come on, boys.

695
00:57:25,265 --> 00:57:28,184
The Mets have one out in the fourth,
with a runner on first.

696
00:57:31,522 --> 00:57:33,482
Line drive. Great stab by Robin!

697
00:57:34,525 --> 00:57:37,529
There's the throw to first.
It's a double play!

698
00:57:47,416 --> 00:57:48,667
That a boy. Here you go.

699
00:57:51,337 --> 00:57:53,631
Luck don't last forever, lawn boy.

700
00:57:57,010 --> 00:57:59,430
It's all right, man. It's all right.
Stay focused.

701
00:58:03,935 --> 00:58:06,813
Ryan Dunne's in a bit of a jam
here in the sixth.

702
00:58:06,939 --> 00:58:12,153
I don't believe he and the catcher, Brubaker
are seeing eye-to-eye on pitch selection.

703
00:58:18,536 --> 00:58:20,412
Just outside. Ball four.

704
00:58:21,497 --> 00:58:23,249
Come on, blue, what was that?

705
00:58:24,209 --> 00:58:26,461
Doyle trots to first,
and that will load them up.

706
00:58:26,712 --> 00:58:28,923
Get off your knees, man,
you're blowing the game.

707
00:58:29,048 --> 00:58:30,632
Did you say something, son?

708
00:58:31,175 --> 00:58:34,351
No, sir, he didn't. Come on, Ry.

709
00:58:34,470 --> 00:58:38,932
This is the kind of situation where
Dunne has become undone in the past.

710
00:58:41,563 --> 00:58:44,732
I'm just trying to figure out
what inning you'll self-destruct.

711
00:58:46,443 --> 00:58:49,071
Fastball plunks him in the back.

712
00:58:50,406 --> 00:58:52,757
One big mistake.

713
00:59:00,460 --> 00:59:01,502
Time.

714
00:59:17,063 --> 00:59:19,356
Does his wife know he's 
screwing us?

715
00:59:20,524 --> 00:59:22,651
Let's not have a meltdown out here.

716
00:59:23,362 --> 00:59:25,155
- It's me.
- What?

717
00:59:26,448 --> 00:59:29,785
I don't think he appreciates
me farting in his face all night.

718
00:59:30,119 --> 00:59:33,163
First, it was accidental.
Now I'm trying to make him cry.

719
00:59:33,414 --> 00:59:37,502
I just dropped a bomb back there and I'm
pretty sure I just poo-pooed in my panties.

720
00:59:39,838 --> 00:59:42,049
All right. Bear down.

721
00:59:45,679 --> 00:59:49,058
Right now, we're playing catch, all right?
Just play catch. Come on now.

722
00:59:49,725 --> 00:59:51,560
Dunne trying to regain his composure.

723
00:59:51,602 --> 00:59:55,898
One run already in, and the bases
are still loaded with one out here in the sixth.

724
01:00:00,863 --> 01:00:02,656
And there's a wild pitch.

725
01:00:09,915 --> 01:00:13,210
One runner scores and here comes Doyle,
all the way from second.

726
01:00:14,965 --> 01:00:18,216
- Safe. He's safe.
- Come on!

727
01:00:22,054 --> 01:00:24,432
Somebody put a quarter
in the merry-go-round.

728
01:00:25,100 --> 01:00:28,435
You got more than that, son.
I'm telling you right now.

729
01:00:30,523 --> 01:00:34,443
What began as a pitchers' duel
turned into a rout...

730
01:00:34,611 --> 01:00:37,305
as the A's fall to the Hyannis Mets,
8 to nothing.

731
01:00:39,575 --> 01:00:41,536
There he is. Can you sign this?

732
01:00:46,333 --> 01:00:47,376
Thank you.

733
01:00:50,796 --> 01:00:51,838
Thank you.

734
01:00:52,883 --> 01:00:56,928
Ryan, this is Hugh Alexander.
He's the scout for the Phillies.

735
01:00:57,137 --> 01:01:00,482
That's good stuff out there.
You stay focused now.

736
01:01:01,872 --> 01:01:03,055
Thank you.

737
01:01:04,228 --> 01:01:07,523
They need to see you pitch again,
they're interested in you. He told me.

738
01:01:11,738 --> 01:01:14,115
I'm in the bullpen from here out...

739
01:01:14,699 --> 01:01:17,869
next to Calvin Knight
who's the best closer in the League.

740
01:01:19,956 --> 01:01:21,916
That ump, he had it in for you.

741
01:01:22,249 --> 01:01:23,709
You deserve better.

742
01:01:29,717 --> 01:01:30,926
Thanks, Dad.

743
01:01:42,148 --> 01:01:47,149
So I don't think I'll even show up
for the last couple of games.

744
01:01:49,323 --> 01:01:50,365
What?

745
01:01:53,203 --> 01:01:58,165
Come on. Every scout was all over that 
Hyannis kid who hit the slam off me.

746
01:01:58,835 --> 01:02:01,912
Yeah, he'll be getting
a wicked big check come spring.

747
01:02:02,714 --> 01:02:05,006
Yeah, I'm going to get a check, too.

748
01:02:04,986 --> 01:02:07,936
About $70 for cutting grass
at Chatham Elementary.

749
01:02:08,220 --> 01:02:11,182
Come on, Ry.
I think you're a really good pitcher.

750
01:02:12,976 --> 01:02:15,144
What you think don't mean shit.

751
01:02:17,757 --> 01:02:18,607
What?

752
01:02:19,363 --> 01:02:23,964
All that matters is making it,
getting signed and cashing a check.

753
01:02:23,822 --> 01:02:26,292
Right now I'm lucky...

754
01:02:26,247 --> 01:02:30,978
if some scrub team in Podunk lets me pitch
batting practice for the next couple of season.

755
01:02:30,982 --> 01:02:32,066
You're wrong.

756
01:02:31,581 --> 01:02:33,666
Bullshit! That's all that matters.

757
01:02:33,791 --> 01:02:37,378
It's not bullshit. What matters is that some 
of us would say you've already made it.

758
01:02:37,504 --> 01:02:39,964
Some of us who've been there for you...

759
01:02:40,132 --> 01:02:44,094
who drove to Boston College to see you pitch
and went to Framingham state,...

760
01:02:44,318 --> 01:02:46,420
and sat at your mom's wake with you.

761
01:02:46,348 --> 01:02:49,602
And cleaned you up behind the Oasis
when you couldn't pick yourself up out off ground.

762
01:02:49,727 --> 01:02:53,231
And who let you live with me
when you and your old man were at it.

763
01:02:53,565 --> 01:02:57,569
Yeah, we matter. I matter.
You bet your ass what I think matters.

764
01:02:58,905 --> 01:03:00,907
I didn't miss one game, Ry. 

765
01:03:01,324 --> 01:03:02,700
Not one game.

766
01:03:03,034 --> 01:03:07,325
And I'm proud as hell
you've done what you've done.

767
01:03:07,224 --> 01:03:11,775
When you hit that mound,
I keep from crying,...

768
01:03:11,002 --> 01:03:16,331
thinking about what we've been through.
Me, and him, and your father, and Mike.

769
01:03:16,717 --> 01:03:19,428
None of us has missed a game.

770
01:03:21,597 --> 01:03:23,766
This ain't just about a paycheck, Ry.

771
01:03:26,269 --> 01:03:30,107
It's about having pride in 
what you do.

772
01:03:30,274 --> 01:03:34,234
Because I do.

773
01:03:34,237 --> 01:03:36,914
- All right, Auggie.
- No, Pete.

774
01:03:38,909 --> 01:03:43,430
If Podunk invites you
you're gonna go.

775
01:03:43,665 --> 01:03:47,127
And I'm going too, and Pete's coming.
Right, Pete?

776
01:03:47,461 --> 01:03:48,803
Yeah, I'll go.

777
01:03:52,968 --> 01:03:57,238
To Podunk.

778
01:03:57,931 --> 01:04:00,016
- Come on.
- To Podunk.

779
01:04:05,065 --> 01:04:07,692
I love you, man. 
You're my best friend.

780
01:04:08,777 --> 01:04:10,069
You're my best friend.

781
01:04:14,075 --> 01:04:17,079
I love you, too, Pete.
Pete's our best friend, too.

782
01:04:21,625 --> 01:04:23,669
I'm starting to like this girl.

783
01:04:28,968 --> 01:04:32,763
Girl looks like that and cuts your grass,
what else do you need?

784
01:04:32,930 --> 01:04:36,909
She could have beers in a cooler
hanging from her neck, but that's just me.

785
01:04:38,354 --> 01:04:39,938
Get out there, son.

786
01:04:46,947 --> 01:04:49,074
My parents are having 
a party tonight.

787
01:04:49,158 --> 01:04:49,867
What?

788
01:04:50,368 --> 01:04:55,122
My parents are having a party tonight
and you should come.

789
01:04:55,624 --> 01:04:59,378
Oh, yeah. Me and your dad 
are real tight.

790
01:05:01,547 --> 01:05:06,243
I told him about us. He was the one
that insisted that you come.

791
01:05:07,429 --> 01:05:10,741
I told Chris, too. 
He left last night.

792
01:05:13,770 --> 01:05:16,522
I got creamed by Hyannis 
last night.

793
01:05:16,992 --> 01:05:22,329
Yeah, Katie said.
You and the umpire. I'm sorry.

794
01:05:22,321 --> 01:05:25,616
That's okay.
I'm out of the starting rotation.

795
01:05:26,118 --> 01:05:29,705
I mean, I'll pitch some relief,
but it's kind of over.

796
01:05:30,039 --> 01:05:35,962
Listen. I did everything wrong with us.
I should have told you about Chris.

797
01:05:36,505 --> 01:05:39,705
And this war with my father
has been going on for four years...

798
01:05:39,899 --> 01:05:41,500
and it's finally out of control.

799
01:05:43,138 --> 01:05:44,347
Forget it.

800
01:05:44,597 --> 01:05:50,344
No. I was confused and I dragged you
into the middle of my mess.

801
01:05:53,775 --> 01:05:57,236
You're the only one who really cares
about what I want.

802
01:06:04,037 --> 01:06:05,080
Thank you.

803
01:06:08,876 --> 01:06:10,670
The summer is almost over...

804
01:06:10,879 --> 01:06:14,156
and the one thing I'm not confused about
is that I want to see you.

805
01:06:15,884 --> 01:06:17,761
I don't have a game tonight.

806
01:06:18,095 --> 01:06:21,598
Come anytime after 5:00.
The party goes all night.

807
01:06:23,685 --> 01:06:24,852
I'll try.

808
01:06:35,991 --> 01:06:39,851
Don't forget to do the trim, okay?

809
01:06:42,040 --> 01:06:44,709
Yeah, and I'll make sure
to mow the flower bed.

810
01:06:45,460 --> 01:06:48,297
If I can find the bird feeder,
I guess I'll mow that, too.

811
01:06:48,506 --> 01:06:50,757
That's funny.
That's very funny.

812
01:06:51,425 --> 01:06:52,467
Come here.

813
01:07:02,397 --> 01:07:05,692
If this party gets too boring,
and I can tell right now that it won't...

814
01:07:05,984 --> 01:07:08,403
the team is having this party 
at the Oasis.

815
01:07:08,654 --> 01:07:13,034
Tenley Parrish. I haven't seen you
in years. Look at you!

816
01:07:13,326 --> 01:07:15,328
Excuse me.
I'll meet you at the bar.

817
01:07:17,248 --> 01:07:20,459
The last time I saw you,
you had just gotten back from Europe.

818
01:07:23,714 --> 01:07:25,424
Beer, please.

819
01:07:25,981 --> 01:07:27,166
Hey, Ryan.

820
01:07:26,967 --> 01:07:31,138
Hey, Katie. It's nice to see you
out of your mascot uniforms.

821
01:07:31,764 --> 01:07:35,143
The mascot search is over. 
Nobody gets it.

822
01:07:36,024 --> 01:07:37,068
I quit.

823
01:07:36,603 --> 01:07:40,858
Don't quit. You just have to figure out
the true spirit of Chatham.

824
01:07:41,317 --> 01:07:42,943
Trust your heart on this one.

825
01:07:43,588 --> 01:07:44,859
Hello, Ryan.

826
01:07:44,446 --> 01:07:48,000
I'm glad you came.
You look very nice tonight.

827
01:07:48,083 --> 01:07:49,334
Thank you, Mrs. Parrish.

828
01:07:49,973 --> 01:07:51,849
Make yourself at home.

829
01:07:52,163 --> 01:07:55,392
Hey, Ryan. Glad you could make it.
How are you?

830
01:07:55,310 --> 01:07:57,310
- Walk with me, will you?
- Yes, sir.

831
01:08:01,841 --> 01:08:04,301
I need you to understand something.

832
01:08:04,636 --> 01:08:07,889
I know this is difficult, 
but let's be realistic.

833
01:08:08,432 --> 01:08:13,371
We both know this little fling you're having
is going to be over by Labor Day anyway.

834
01:08:13,521 --> 01:08:15,356
So, I need your help.

835
01:08:17,151 --> 01:08:19,736
I want Tenley to focus on her future.

836
01:08:21,405 --> 01:08:22,698
Alone.

837
01:08:24,993 --> 01:08:28,437
I've known your father a long time.
He's a good man.

838
01:08:29,040 --> 01:08:31,625
What does my dad have to do 
with this?

839
01:08:31,751 --> 01:08:36,406
I don't want to see anybody get hurt.
But you've stepped over a boundary here, son.

840
01:08:36,382 --> 01:08:38,342
A boundary? What boundary?

841
01:08:38,634 --> 01:08:42,680
You know damn well what the boundaries are here.
They're as old as Chatham itself.

842
01:08:42,806 --> 01:08:44,474
What are you trying to tell me?

843
01:08:45,350 --> 01:08:47,644
Along with a number of my friends...

844
01:08:47,812 --> 01:08:51,148
I'd have to take a good hard look
at our arrangements with your father.

845
01:08:52,693 --> 01:08:53,819
What?

846
01:08:55,904 --> 01:08:58,757
- Ryan, I'm thinking of you here.
- Yeah.

847
01:08:59,867 --> 01:09:04,155
And I'm thinking of you, Rand,
when I say you can take this lawn job...

848
01:09:04,145 --> 01:09:05,746
and shove it up your ass.

849
01:09:07,167 --> 01:09:11,079
He'll be here tomorrow. 
I guarantee.

850
01:09:18,055 --> 01:09:19,514
I'll be right back.

851
01:09:23,520 --> 01:09:24,938
Where are you going?

852
01:09:29,819 --> 01:09:33,322
Just meet me tomorrow night
at the field after the game.

853
01:09:57,184 --> 01:09:59,270
Rand Parrish said that?

854
01:10:00,480 --> 01:10:05,026
Sometimes parents get too involved
and say stuff they don't mean.

855
01:10:06,195 --> 01:10:10,073
Forget about it.
You were probably right about Tenley.

856
01:10:13,495 --> 01:10:15,663
I was really in the bag the other night.

857
01:10:17,958 --> 01:10:19,709
I said some dumb things.

858
01:10:22,254 --> 01:10:27,593
The right girl, family,
last you forever.

859
01:10:37,773 --> 01:10:40,943
Your mother used to say
the reason the Indian rain dance worked...

860
01:10:41,027 --> 01:10:45,156
is because they wouldn't 
stop dancing until it rained.

861
01:10:46,784 --> 01:10:49,328
Every time it rained, she'd say that.

862
01:10:53,542 --> 01:10:55,043
Yeah. I remember.

863
01:10:59,966 --> 01:11:01,467
Stay at it.

864
01:11:04,178 --> 01:11:07,140
You're a good kid, a good ball player.

865
01:11:07,766 --> 01:11:10,059
Baseball might be a career for you.

866
01:11:21,490 --> 01:11:22,867
I would never.

867
01:11:23,535 --> 01:11:25,953
Come on, Dale. Giddy up. 

868
01:11:26,496 --> 01:11:28,832
- Where are you going?
- To get a better view.

869
01:11:29,501 --> 01:11:32,586
Come on, Tenley.
Are you staying in Chatham?

870
01:11:32,670 --> 01:11:35,490
Or if I get a tryout somewhere,
are you going to follow me around?

871
01:11:36,884 --> 01:11:38,802
You're going to San Francisco.

872
01:11:39,762 --> 01:11:42,766
If I don't like the job,
maybe I'll just go to graduate school.

873
01:11:45,018 --> 01:11:46,937
You can go to grad school 
anywhere.

874
01:11:51,424 --> 01:11:52,725
One, two, four!

875
01:11:57,908 --> 01:12:01,853
- Ladies, Chatham's finest.
- All right.

876
01:12:02,204 --> 01:12:03,872
Our pride and joy.

877
01:12:03,873 --> 01:12:05,542
I'm ever honored!

878
01:12:08,003 --> 01:12:09,421
Thank you, my prince.

879
01:12:15,345 --> 01:12:16,555
Night-night.

880
01:12:17,181 --> 01:12:19,057
Careful up there, you two.

881
01:12:25,816 --> 01:12:29,195
You're not listening to me. My father 
won't pay for grad school in architecture.

882
01:12:29,362 --> 01:12:31,280
So what? You can get loans.

883
01:12:31,364 --> 01:12:33,074
You don't understand.

884
01:12:33,491 --> 01:12:35,911
Understand what, being broke?
I understand.

885
01:12:36,366 --> 01:12:37,616
- No.
- What?

886
01:12:38,030 --> 01:12:41,343
Doing something you love? 
I understand.

887
01:12:41,584 --> 01:12:45,129
I love standing on that mound
with a baseball in my hand...

888
01:12:45,547 --> 01:12:48,384
staring at a guy
holding a club 60 feet away...

889
01:12:48,551 --> 01:12:51,345
knowing that he can't touch me.

890
01:12:53,932 --> 01:12:57,852
It is the only place in the world
where I feel powerful.

891
01:13:00,440 --> 01:13:04,695
Shit!
I'll probably end up cutting grass.

892
01:13:05,487 --> 01:13:09,741
- Why are you so scared?
- Scared of what?

893
01:13:09,825 --> 01:13:14,946
Of everything. 
Success. Love.

894
01:13:15,790 --> 01:13:20,220
You say you love being out on that mound.
Why would you ever settle for cutting grass?

895
01:13:20,713 --> 01:13:23,925
Wait a second, who's scared?
I can't control my career, you can.

896
01:13:24,134 --> 01:13:26,272
If you love architecture so much,...

897
01:13:26,191 --> 01:13:28,492
why are you going to settle
for the life your daddy set up for you?

898
01:13:29,974 --> 01:13:32,067
What do you want me to do?

899
01:13:36,857 --> 01:13:41,220
Get on a plane.
Go to San Francisco.

900
01:13:41,651 --> 01:13:42,995
- What?
- This is never...

901
01:13:44,198 --> 01:13:45,449
Shit!

902
01:13:45,700 --> 01:13:47,119
Why did you lock the door?

903
01:13:47,203 --> 01:13:48,329
Get down here!

904
01:13:55,121 --> 01:13:57,032
Van Leemer and Lauren are still 
locked upstairs!

905
01:13:57,004 --> 01:13:58,903
I got them! Get out!

906
01:14:06,266 --> 01:14:07,608
Get out of here!

907
01:14:21,366 --> 01:14:23,410
- Are you okay?
- Yeah, I'm okay.

908
01:14:33,381 --> 01:14:36,426
A's Press Box set ablaze.

909
01:14:36,844 --> 01:14:40,380
"Tenley Parrish,
daughter of Rand and Victoria Parrish...

910
01:14:40,377 --> 01:14:42,577
and A's pitcher, Ryan Dunne...

911
01:14:42,577 --> 01:14:44,377
watched firemen extinguish a blaze...

912
01:14:44,376 --> 01:14:47,477
that engulfed the new
Veterans Field press box last night."

913
01:14:47,565 --> 01:14:53,120
Thank you. Congratulations, your 
humiliation of this family is complete.

914
01:14:54,120 --> 01:14:56,080
We had nothing to do
with starting that fire.

915
01:14:56,247 --> 01:14:59,918
You were there.
It's all part of this goddamn situation.

916
01:15:00,294 --> 01:15:05,842
This kid is going to end up back here
cutting grass with his old man guaranteed!

917
01:15:06,384 --> 01:15:08,886
Who are you to judge
what he does with his life?

918
01:15:08,970 --> 01:15:11,807
Ryan is going to do whatever it takes
to make it in baseball!

919
01:15:12,349 --> 01:15:14,225
Fine, go with him. 
Go with him, then.

920
01:15:18,773 --> 01:15:21,233
He doesn't want me to go 
with him!

921
01:15:23,738 --> 01:15:27,241
I'm going to San Francisco
to work for Uncle Richard.

922
01:15:29,244 --> 01:15:32,780
Aren't you happy, Dad?
You win, okay?

923
01:15:39,255 --> 01:15:41,341
Why stop with the press box?

924
01:15:41,800 --> 01:15:45,220
If you're going to start fires,
why don't you burn down Main Street?

925
01:15:47,599 --> 01:15:50,226
The League commissioner
wanted to call this game off.

926
01:15:50,352 --> 01:15:53,481
I had to convince her
that to penalize the rest of the team...

927
01:15:53,564 --> 01:15:57,150
for the stupidity of a couple
of knuckleheads would be unfair.

928
01:15:58,570 --> 01:16:02,257
But Robin and Van Leemer,
they're ghosts.

929
01:16:02,245 --> 01:16:03,189
Ghosts!

930
01:16:04,369 --> 01:16:07,080
I packed their asses on the bus
this morning.

931
01:16:07,246 --> 01:16:10,583
Which means we finish the regular season
and go into the playoffs...

932
01:16:10,709 --> 01:16:14,546
without our number one pitcher
and our starting shortstop.

933
01:16:14,797 --> 01:16:17,675
Look at me when I'm talking to you,
goddamn it!

934
01:16:21,721 --> 01:16:25,350
Tomorrow at 4:00 p.m.
Dunne...

935
01:16:27,353 --> 01:16:31,524
you've got the freshest arm.
You get to start tomorrow.

936
01:16:32,276 --> 01:16:35,989
Now get the hell out of my sight,
I'm sick of looking at you. Move.

937
01:16:55,720 --> 01:16:58,473
Sean, I thought I asked you
not to park in the driveway?

938
01:16:58,557 --> 01:17:00,809
I just came by to give you a final bill.

939
01:17:01,310 --> 01:17:05,398
A final bill? What about the fall?
We've got leaves and...

940
01:17:05,523 --> 01:17:08,400
John Kroft's crew does good work.
I'll put him in touch.

941
01:17:08,860 --> 01:17:11,822
Now wait a minute. Sean.
What are you doing?

942
01:17:16,745 --> 01:17:19,122
My boy told me what you said.

943
01:17:20,373 --> 01:17:23,752
Pride isn't exclusive to you people
on Shore Road, Mr. Parrish.

944
01:17:24,712 --> 01:17:26,004
Good day.

945
01:17:33,513 --> 01:17:34,515
Shit.

946
01:17:38,478 --> 01:17:39,687
Come in.

947
01:17:46,363 --> 01:17:47,906
I've been waiting for you.

948
01:17:48,615 --> 01:17:50,366
Come on in. Sit down.

949
01:17:52,495 --> 01:17:55,289
Come on, don't be bashful.

950
01:18:04,926 --> 01:18:06,719
Let's talk.

951
01:18:08,388 --> 01:18:14,269
Baseball is a game
full of legends and lore.

952
01:18:16,230 --> 01:18:19,484
I'm just another baseball legend, 
Domo.

953
01:18:25,199 --> 01:18:28,035
I know you've heard
some stories about me.

954
01:18:28,202 --> 01:18:29,954
Some of them are true.

955
01:18:34,294 --> 01:18:36,602
You can tell your own stories.

956
01:18:36,602 --> 01:18:39,002
But I can help you
with your baseball career.

957
01:18:42,469 --> 01:18:44,846
I'm real good with ball players.

958
01:18:47,726 --> 01:18:48,977
Really?

959
01:18:52,315 --> 01:18:54,317
See the basket at the end 
of the bed?

960
01:18:56,736 --> 01:18:57,536
Yes.

961
01:18:58,572 --> 01:19:00,240
Hand me the cucumber.

962
01:19:05,955 --> 01:19:08,165
Domo! Domo! Domo!

963
01:19:15,174 --> 01:19:17,010
- It was gone.
- The whole thing?

964
01:19:17,802 --> 01:19:19,361
No way. An entire 
cucumber?

965
01:19:20,138 --> 01:19:22,975
I swear, it was like
Guinness Book of Records type stuff.

966
01:19:23,893 --> 01:19:25,477
I'm happy for you, kid.

967
01:19:27,688 --> 01:19:28,731
Bru, what's wrong, man?

968
01:19:29,650 --> 01:19:31,860
I was there for lunch today.

969
01:19:32,194 --> 01:19:34,697
She made me a cucumber salad.

970
01:19:43,047 --> 01:19:45,447
- Hey.
- Hey.

971
01:19:49,438 --> 01:19:52,691
I'm...I'm starting tomorrow.

972
01:19:53,735 --> 01:19:57,972
Yeah, I heard. Falmouth, right?
Good luck.

973
01:20:01,157 --> 01:20:04,878
Every scout in the League is goin' to be there
expecting to see Van Leemer versus Huber.

974
01:20:06,708 --> 01:20:10,462
I know. You're going to pitch 
a great game and get discovered.

975
01:20:16,303 --> 01:20:17,721
I'm scared, Mike.

976
01:20:21,892 --> 01:20:25,187
This is it.

977
01:20:25,646 --> 01:20:28,441
You'll be fine, just pitch your game.

978
01:20:31,028 --> 01:20:32,529
What's my game?

979
01:20:37,952 --> 01:20:39,411
You're really asking me?

980
01:20:43,084 --> 01:20:46,922
- You're really asking me.
- Come on, Mike.

981
01:20:50,342 --> 01:20:51,384
Sit down.

982
01:20:59,478 --> 01:21:03,607
Hit your spots. Don't try to blow fastballs
by every guy that gets in the box.

983
01:21:04,108 --> 01:21:06,111
But I can throw way over 90.

984
01:21:06,194 --> 01:21:10,031
Everybody in the minor league system
can throw 90-plus. So what?

985
01:21:10,282 --> 01:21:13,493
When is the last time
Greg Maddux threw 95?

986
01:21:13,911 --> 01:21:16,205
- I want to be intimidating.
- Come on.

987
01:21:17,457 --> 01:21:19,876
Wouldn't you rather be rich?

988
01:21:23,131 --> 01:21:26,641
You are so stubborn.
You're just like Mom: bullheaded.

989
01:21:26,675 --> 01:21:29,276
You place your fastball,
throw your curves for strikes.

990
01:21:29,295 --> 01:21:30,993
You're dangerous, Ryan.

991
01:21:30,918 --> 01:21:33,218
You are. You're as good
as any of those guys out there.

992
01:21:34,978 --> 01:21:36,069
Come on.

993
01:21:38,523 --> 01:21:40,275
Believe in yourself.

994
01:21:46,825 --> 01:21:49,285
Mom was pretty stubborn.

995
01:21:52,498 --> 01:21:55,834
She made me drive her to that game
you pitched against UMass.

996
01:21:56,669 --> 01:21:58,738
She was sick as a dog.

997
01:22:00,674 --> 01:22:02,634
Yeah, she never missed a game 
back then.

998
01:22:06,848 --> 01:22:08,808
She hasn't missed one since.

999
01:22:13,606 --> 01:22:14,982
Come on, I'll buy you a beer.

1000
01:22:19,529 --> 01:22:22,449
She's so fat, if she wore high heels,
she'd strike oil.

1001
01:22:25,453 --> 01:22:27,913
What did the one fat chick
say to the other fat chick?

1002
01:22:28,415 --> 01:22:30,291
- What?
- Who cares? They're fat.

1003
01:22:34,672 --> 01:22:35,672
Fat chicks are cool.

1004
01:22:35,649 --> 01:22:39,777
They're like mopeds, fun to ride,
just don't let your friends see you do it.

1005
01:22:41,597 --> 01:22:45,434
That's it. Hey, you know what?
I've got something to say.

1006
01:22:45,935 --> 01:22:47,145
Listen up.

1007
01:22:47,896 --> 01:22:49,105
Excuse me.

1008
01:22:49,190 --> 01:22:51,858
Can I have everybody's attention
for one minute?

1009
01:22:51,942 --> 01:22:53,736
There's something
I need to say to everybody.

1010
01:22:55,571 --> 01:23:00,868
My name is Miles Dalrymple
and I'm tired of living a lie.

1011
01:23:02,871 --> 01:23:07,459
I need it to be known
that I like a big girl.

1012
01:23:09,003 --> 01:23:15,218
In fact, a large, zaftig,
voluptuous, full-figured, big-boned...

1013
01:23:15,872 --> 01:23:17,373
massive-assive honey.

1014
01:23:19,141 --> 01:23:21,226
That is what really gets me going!

1015
01:23:21,893 --> 01:23:26,315
I like fat women and they like me!
Anybody got a problem with that?

1016
01:23:32,823 --> 01:23:35,368
Big girls need love too, baby!

1017
01:23:39,045 --> 01:23:41,046
- Hi.
- Hey.

1018
01:23:43,051 --> 01:23:44,719
Just like old times.

1019
01:23:44,738 --> 01:23:47,365
Yeah. I didn't see you in there.

1020
01:23:48,432 --> 01:23:50,809
I was home, packing.

1021
01:23:54,314 --> 01:23:56,399
I'm going to San Francisco tomorrow.

1022
01:24:10,834 --> 01:24:13,710
- Do you want to sit down?
- Yeah.

1023
01:24:22,347 --> 01:24:24,265
I'm pitching tomorrow.

1024
01:24:28,396 --> 01:24:32,733
I had a huge fight with my father.
I can't stay here with him.

1025
01:24:34,862 --> 01:24:36,154
About what?

1026
01:24:42,078 --> 01:24:43,329
You.

1027
01:24:53,633 --> 01:24:54,884
When are you leaving?

1028
01:24:56,762 --> 01:24:58,765
Tomorrow night.

1029
01:25:05,568 --> 01:25:07,568
- Just as well...
- We're better off...

1030
01:25:14,699 --> 01:25:18,161
Let yourself be great 
tomorrow night.

1031
01:25:28,466 --> 01:25:30,384
I'm really going to miss you.

1032
01:25:59,210 --> 01:26:03,110
Ahoy, mateys.
I am the true spirit of Chatham...

1033
01:26:03,086 --> 01:26:05,881
a drunken fisherman
named Barnacle Barb.

1034
01:26:06,459 --> 01:26:08,101
I like to drink.

1035
01:26:09,346 --> 01:26:11,223
I like to fight.

1036
01:26:12,559 --> 01:26:16,188
I like to fall down in pools
of my own vomit!

1037
01:26:19,275 --> 01:26:22,612
Tonight, the Chatham A's
take on the Falmouth Commodores.

1038
01:26:22,779 --> 01:26:24,821
And a last-minute pitching change...

1039
01:26:24,821 --> 01:26:26,821
the A's will send
Ryan Dunne to the mound.

1040
01:26:27,443 --> 01:26:28,294
Ryan!

1041
01:26:33,583 --> 01:26:34,835
Get them, tiger!

1042
01:26:34,918 --> 01:26:37,337
I'm proud as hell
you've done what you've done.

1043
01:26:38,042 --> 01:26:40,012
Dunne replaces Eric Van Leemer...

1044
01:26:40,153 --> 01:26:43,153
who proved to be even more
of a flamethrower than we imagined.

1045
01:26:43,887 --> 01:26:46,557
It's a good opportunity for the 
young lefty,...

1046
01:26:46,724 --> 01:26:49,059
after being banished to the bullpen
by coach Schiffner.

1047
01:26:50,269 --> 01:26:52,939
That's good stuff out there.
You stay focused now.

1048
01:27:02,325 --> 01:27:04,372
Swing and a miss. Strike three.

1049
01:27:04,372 --> 01:27:05,623
Number one, Ry dog!

1050
01:27:07,122 --> 01:27:10,850
Then one day you have this moment
where it all just arrives. Everything clicks.

1051
01:27:13,880 --> 01:27:15,202
He struck him out.

1052
01:27:15,202 --> 01:27:16,002
2.6.

1053
01:27:20,387 --> 01:27:22,089
Got him on a good breaking ball.

1054
01:27:25,811 --> 01:27:28,981
I'm just trying to figure out
what inning you'll self-destruct.

1055
01:27:29,065 --> 01:27:34,953
The question with Dunne has always been, 
can he keep it together for a whole ball game?

1056
01:27:36,573 --> 01:27:38,783
That's four K's for Dunne.

1057
01:27:44,874 --> 01:27:46,555
You are dangerous, Ryan.

1058
01:27:46,486 --> 01:27:48,886
You are. You're as good
as any of those guys out there.

1059
01:27:51,548 --> 01:27:53,676
One big mistake.

1060
01:27:58,808 --> 01:28:02,894
Swing and a miss. He got him.
That's five strikeouts for Dunne.

1061
01:28:02,895 --> 01:28:06,682
In the middle of the third,
Falmouth is still looking for its first hit.

1062
01:28:09,278 --> 01:28:10,989
I want to stop by the stadium.

1063
01:28:11,072 --> 01:28:14,533
- We really don't have time, Tenley.
- Just for a minute, okay?

1064
01:28:17,371 --> 01:28:21,749
Goose eggs on the board through seven,
but the real story is Ryan Dunne.

1065
01:28:22,210 --> 01:28:26,505
You might want to stay awake for this.
Ryan has got a no-no going.

1066
01:28:28,509 --> 01:28:30,619
Two outs here in the top of 
the eighth.

1067
01:28:33,389 --> 01:28:36,308
There's a little looper in the short right 
field, looks like...

1068
01:28:36,310 --> 01:28:39,688
No! Domo makes a circus catch.
What a grab!

1069
01:28:42,859 --> 01:28:46,069
All right! Way to go, Domo!

1070
01:28:46,197 --> 01:28:49,441
The A's second baseman
made a spectacular catch.

1071
01:28:49,867 --> 01:28:52,186
And the Commodores
go down in the eighth.

1072
01:28:54,247 --> 01:28:57,858
Wouldn't you know it, the guy who 
makes the great play in the field...

1073
01:28:57,883 --> 01:29:02,219
now comes in to lead off for his team 
at bat in the last of the eighth inning.

1074
01:29:01,380 --> 01:29:04,700
Get on now. Make them 
pitch to you.

1075
01:29:04,635 --> 01:29:07,237
Mickey "Domo" Dominguez
stands in against Huber.

1076
01:29:10,975 --> 01:29:13,185
There's a liner in the right. 
Base hit!

1077
01:29:14,321 --> 01:29:16,749
The A's have the lead-off runner
on in the eighth.

1078
01:29:17,695 --> 01:29:21,200
The way these two pitchers are going,
one run may do it tonight.

1079
01:29:25,901 --> 01:29:29,780
On deck for the A's is Billy Brubaker,
who's been hot of late.

1080
01:29:31,241 --> 01:29:33,368
Bru's average is up to .292 now.

1081
01:29:35,955 --> 01:29:37,998
There's a line drive into left
and it's sinking fast.

1082
01:29:38,951 --> 01:29:42,080
McBride can't get it.
It's rolling all the way to the fence.

1083
01:29:42,567 --> 01:29:45,695
Domo is going to score easily.
Brubaker is heading to third.

1084
01:29:47,615 --> 01:29:48,845
He's being waved around.

1085
01:29:48,848 --> 01:29:50,015
Come on, Bru!

1086
01:29:55,769 --> 01:29:56,895
He's safe!

1087
01:29:57,646 --> 01:30:02,482
Inside-the-park homer for Billy Brubaker. And
the A's take a two-run lead here in the eighth.

1088
01:30:10,204 --> 01:30:11,580
Come on now, get up!

1089
01:30:13,934 --> 01:30:17,229
Ryan Dunne will take the mound in the ninth
with a two-run cushion...

1090
01:30:17,397 --> 01:30:20,408
and three outs to go
to complete his masterpiece.

1091
01:30:20,191 --> 01:30:21,692
Be right back.

1092
01:30:26,573 --> 01:30:29,274
Mullin stands in the lead off
with Falmouth in the ninth.

1093
01:30:29,670 --> 01:30:32,172
He's already accounted
for two of Dunne's ten strikeouts.

1094
01:30:37,044 --> 01:30:38,420
Strike one call.

1095
01:30:39,088 --> 01:30:43,034
I just clocked him at 93 mph
in the ninth and he's getting stronger.

1096
01:30:45,724 --> 01:30:49,687
Fastball has got some good velo,
his curve ball shows depth and best of all...

1097
01:30:50,704 --> 01:30:51,784
he's a lefty.

1098
01:30:51,736 --> 01:30:53,447
What is this kid's name, 
anyway?

1099
01:30:55,774 --> 01:30:59,828
Dunne. That's Ryan Dunne.

1100
01:31:00,749 --> 01:31:04,300
- Hi.
- Hi.

1101
01:31:04,785 --> 01:31:06,870
Barnacle Barb is a big hit.

1102
01:31:08,038 --> 01:31:09,706
I thought you were gone.

1103
01:31:09,790 --> 01:31:11,751
I am. 
I just came to say goodbye.

1104
01:31:11,835 --> 01:31:18,033
I don't think he is going to be able 
to hear you. He's got a no-hitter going.

1105
01:31:18,009 --> 01:31:19,135
What's a no-hitter?

1106
01:31:20,762 --> 01:31:23,732
You can't talk about it. 
It will jinx it.

1107
01:31:33,986 --> 01:31:36,113
Let yourself be great.

1108
01:31:45,976 --> 01:31:47,176
Here's the 0-1 pitch.

1109
01:31:47,376 --> 01:31:49,586
Swing and a miss. Strike two.

1110
01:31:50,088 --> 01:31:52,633
I just got him at 95. 
That can't be right.

1111
01:31:52,716 --> 01:31:54,801
It's not. I got 96.

1112
01:32:05,106 --> 01:32:07,533
Swing and a miss. Strike three.

1113
01:32:07,515 --> 01:32:10,466
Dunne pulls the string
on another off-speed breaking ball.

1114
01:32:10,467 --> 01:32:14,681
One up, one down. That's 11 strikeouts
for the hometown left-hander.

1115
01:32:19,622 --> 01:32:23,376
Heaven is number 11!
Two more to go, Ryan!

1116
01:32:23,367 --> 01:32:24,567
Two more! Come on!

1117
01:32:29,920 --> 01:32:31,317
- Bye.
- Bye.

1118
01:32:31,636 --> 01:32:33,512
Two outs to go.

1119
01:32:33,638 --> 01:32:35,589
And now the crowd is on its feet.

1120
01:32:35,595 --> 01:32:38,295
We're really witnessing
something special here tonight.

1121
01:32:50,700 --> 01:32:52,661
Allow yourself to succeed.

1122
01:33:01,254 --> 01:33:02,797
You want big rewards?

1123
01:33:03,715 --> 01:33:05,509
You've got to take big risks.

1124
01:33:10,390 --> 01:33:11,432
Bru!

1125
01:33:13,977 --> 01:33:15,019
Time.

1126
01:33:21,527 --> 01:33:24,315
What's up?
What's going on? You okay?

1127
01:33:24,615 --> 01:33:25,657
I love her.

1128
01:33:28,036 --> 01:33:32,322
Okay, I love her, too,
but let's get two more outs, okay?

1129
01:33:31,706 --> 01:33:33,632
Come on, kid, get up!

1130
01:33:33,834 --> 01:33:35,961
Knight, wake up man.
Get out here!

1131
01:33:36,670 --> 01:33:39,247
- Finish it, Calvin.
- Go on out.

1132
01:33:40,175 --> 01:33:41,634
Auggie, start the car!

1133
01:33:42,135 --> 01:33:43,845
He said start the car.

1134
01:33:43,970 --> 01:33:45,680
Get the cooler. Start the car.

1135
01:33:46,106 --> 01:33:47,406
All right, let's start the car!

1136
01:33:47,767 --> 01:33:49,943
Dude, what are you doing?

1137
01:33:50,895 --> 01:33:54,399
A no-hitter in the Cape League
won't even be in The Globe tomorrow.

1138
01:33:54,650 --> 01:33:57,904
The right girl, that will last you forever.

1139
01:33:59,114 --> 01:34:02,575
Besides, Knight's the best closer
in the League. He's going to finish this.

1140
01:34:02,659 --> 01:34:04,286
Good morning, sunshine.

1141
01:34:04,620 --> 01:34:07,120
Fatty here can't touch a slider...

1142
01:34:07,061 --> 01:34:09,561
and my man on deck
is a sucker for an inside curve. Enjoy!

1143
01:34:10,836 --> 01:34:12,379
Everything all right, fellas?

1144
01:34:12,462 --> 01:34:15,523
- He loves her.
- That's great.

1145
01:34:15,757 --> 01:34:17,342
- Thanks.
- You're welcome.

1146
01:34:18,219 --> 01:34:20,971
- I love her.
- We know.

1147
01:34:20,806 --> 01:34:24,567
Hey, Ryan.
You might want to go this way.

1148
01:34:26,979 --> 01:34:28,447
Go get her!

1149
01:34:29,732 --> 01:34:33,610
This is the damnedest thing
I've seen in 50 years of broadcasting.

1150
01:34:33,611 --> 01:34:39,459
Ryan Dunne is taking himself out of the game
with two outs to go for a no-hitter.

1151
01:34:43,328 --> 01:34:44,428
Ryan, where are we going?

1152
01:34:44,416 --> 01:34:46,502
- I love her.
- Me, too!

1153
01:34:47,003 --> 01:34:48,045
Who?

1154
01:34:48,629 --> 01:34:51,173
- Where?
- To the airport.

1155
01:34:58,401 --> 01:34:59,345
Tenley!

1156
01:35:05,399 --> 01:35:07,200
- I love her.
- What?

1157
01:35:08,110 --> 01:35:09,528
I mean, you.

1158
01:35:10,405 --> 01:35:12,615
- I love you.
- I love you.

1159
01:35:12,949 --> 01:35:16,578
I need to know we are going to be together.
Please don't go to San Francisco.

1160
01:35:16,871 --> 01:35:18,789
I don't want to go to San Francisco.

1161
01:35:18,873 --> 01:35:21,166
Then stay. 
You can go back to school.

1162
01:35:21,250 --> 01:35:23,169
Knight winds and delivers...

1163
01:35:23,462 --> 01:35:25,630
What happened with the no-hitter?

1164
01:35:27,257 --> 01:35:29,009
Allen swings at it. 
It's all over.

1165
01:35:29,719 --> 01:35:32,638
He finished it!
You guys pitched a no-hitter!

1166
01:35:34,183 --> 01:35:36,935
I found it.
I've just pitched the game of my life.

1167
01:35:37,019 --> 01:35:38,311
Let's be together.

1168
01:35:38,437 --> 01:35:40,022
I don't know where. Probably...

1169
01:35:40,106 --> 01:35:42,650
Batavia, New York. 
It's up around Buffalo.

1170
01:35:43,151 --> 01:35:46,530
The Phillies have a Single A team there
called the Batavia Muckdogs.

1171
01:35:46,929 --> 01:35:48,429
- Muckdogs?
- Yeah.

1172
01:35:49,283 --> 01:35:52,161
Mr. Alexander, didn't Ryan earn
a little money tonight?

1173
01:35:53,080 --> 01:35:55,290
Yeah, he sure did.

1174
01:35:56,250 --> 01:36:01,047
In fact, Ryan, I'd like to make you an offer
to play for a Phillies' farm club...

1175
01:36:01,381 --> 01:36:04,184
complete with a guaranteed
$50,000 signing bonus.

1176
01:36:06,011 --> 01:36:07,178
75.

1177
01:36:10,225 --> 01:36:11,392
I beg your pardon?

1178
01:36:11,643 --> 01:36:13,686
$75,000 sounds about right.

1179
01:36:18,276 --> 01:36:20,277
- That would do the trick?
- Yeah!

1180
01:36:20,611 --> 01:36:22,739
Done. Congratulations.

1181
01:36:23,351 --> 01:36:24,451
To the Muckdogs!

1182
01:36:52,859 --> 01:36:57,029
The Phillies are going to bring in
the young left-hander...

1183
01:36:57,012 --> 01:37:00,013
the rookie just brought up
from the minor league, Ryan Dunne.

1184
01:37:00,983 --> 01:37:03,734
Dunne was just called up this week
from Scranton.

1185
01:37:02,911 --> 01:37:06,189
- What's going on over here?
- Man, he's in.

1186
01:37:06,832 --> 01:37:11,419
- He looks good!
- That's good.

1187
01:37:11,250 --> 01:37:15,179
...is none other than the superstar
of the Reds, Ken Griffey, Jr.

1188
01:37:17,428 --> 01:37:21,181
The rookie left-hander Dunne
looks in to his veteran catcher for the sign.

1189
